\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces  Detection performance across all methods at three stealth levels (200 eval samples per class, benign-calibrated threshold: 95th-percentile of held-out benign scores, targeting FPR $\leq $ 0.05). \textbf  {All nine baselines are unsupervised} (benign-only training, 10 seeds); \textbf  {\textsc  {HNIDS}{} conditions A--D are supervised} (labeled hard negatives or Gaussian-noise negatives provided during training, 10 seeds matching Table~\ref {tab:ablation}). See Appendix~\ref {app:supervision} for the supervision discussion. \textbf  {Bold}: best calibrated (non-degenerate) value per column. \underline  {Underline}: second-best calibrated value per column. Threshold IDS and Statistical IDS are marked $\ddagger $: their high F1 arises from near-total FP assignment (FPR $>$ 0.87), not genuine stealth detection. Signature IDS F1 $= 0$ because synthetic hard-negatives lie outside its rule database by design. Bold/underline exclude zero-shot A (near-chance detection, AUC$=$0.481). $\dagger $ marks our proposed system; Table~\ref {tab:ablation} gives the full ablation. }}{7}{table.caption.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:main}{{1}{7}{Detection performance across all methods at three stealth levels (200 eval samples per class, benign-calibrated threshold: 95th-percentile of held-out benign scores, targeting FPR $\leq $ 0.05). \textbf {All nine baselines are unsupervised} (benign-only training, 10 seeds); \textbf {\ours {} conditions A--D are supervised} (labeled hard negatives or Gaussian-noise negatives provided during training, 10 seeds matching Table~\ref {tab:ablation}). See Appendix~\ref {app:supervision} for the supervision discussion. \textbf {Bold}: best calibrated (non-degenerate) value per column. \underline {Underline}: second-best calibrated value per column. Threshold IDS and Statistical IDS are marked $\ddagger $: their high F1 arises from near-total FP assignment (FPR $>$ 0.87), not genuine stealth detection. Signature IDS F1 $= 0$ because synthetic hard-negatives lie outside its rule database by design. Bold/underline exclude zero-shot A (near-chance detection, AUC$=$0.481). $\dagger $ marks our proposed system; Table~\ref {tab:ablation} gives the full ablation}{table.caption.2}{}}
\newlabel{sec:experiments:constraints}{{5.3}{7}{Ablation Study}{table.caption.3}{}}
